\cline{2-6}
x + 1 & x^5 & & & & +7 \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{-x^5} & -x^4 & & & \\
\cline{2-3}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{0} & -x^4 & & & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & +x^4 & +x^3 & & \\
\cline{3-4}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & -x^3 & +x^2 & \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & +x^3 & +x^2 & \\
\cline{4-5}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & -2x^2 & +x \\
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & +2x^2 & +2x \\
\cline{5-6}
\multicolumn{2}{r}{} & & & & -x + 7 \\
\end{array}$
The quotient is $x^4 - x^3 + x^2 - x + 1$, so the answer is $\boxed{x^4 - x^3 + x^2 - x + 1}$.The answer is x^4-x^3+x^2-x+1

