Since the slope of the line passing through $(1,1)$ and $(x,x^2)$ is $\frac{x^2 - 1}{x - 1} = x + 1,$ we have
\[x + 1 = -\frac{1}{2}.\]Solving, we find $x = -\frac{3}{2},$ so $B = \boxed{\left( -\frac{3}{2}, \frac{9}{4} \right)}.$The answer is (-\frac{3}{2},\frac{9}{4})

