draw((0,-10)--(0,10));
draw((5,1)--(D),dashed);

dot("$5 + i$", A, E);
dot("$1 - 2i$", B, NW);
dot("$9 + 4i$", C, NE);
dot(D);
[/asy]

Also, the distance between the centers of the circles centered at $5 + i$ and $9 + 4i$ is $|4 - 3i| = 5$.
Therefore, the circles centered at $5 + i$ and $9 + 4i$ are also tangent to each other.

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

pair A, B, C, D;

A = (5,1);
B = (1,2);
C = (9,-4);
D = (5,-3);

draw(Circle(A,5));
draw(Circle(B,5));
draw(Circle(C,5));
